n| `src-tauri/src/run/resume/orchestration.rs` | Resume orchestration functions including pre-confirmation ingest helpers, terminal disposition handlers, unconfirmed delivery handlers, delivery-confirmation predicates, hashing formatter, resume target validators/mappers, migration helpers, and terminal-signal helpers | Source lines 97-1545; diff hunks 737-972 | exactly one per symbol: orchestration, predicate, accessor, mapper, validator, formatter, parser, or filter | LOW | Changed `ingest_mailbox_delivery_confirmation_turn_if_needed` is pure orchestration over named confirmation predicates and targeted session scanning. `mailbox_delivery_unconfirmed`, `mailbox_delivery_requires_turn_confirmation`, `mailbox_delivery_turn_confirmed`, `submitted_user_turn_confirms_mailbox_delivery`, `submitted_user_turn_payload_confirms_mailbox_delivery`, and `ingested_user_turn_confirms_mailbox_delivery` each answer one boolean question. Error emission and digest formatting remain separate formatter helpers. |\n| `src-tauri/src/run_tauri.rs` | `run_tauri`, `default_models_dir`, `runtime_paths_for` | Source lines 30-99; diff hunk 30-35 | exactly one per symbol: orchestration, accessor, or mapper | LOW | Changed `run_tauri` remains bootstrap orchestration and only adds the named wake maintenance-driver start before service construction. `default_models_dir` accesses a configured/default path, and `runtime_paths_for` maps path inputs into a `RuntimePaths` struct. |\n| `src-tauri/src/wake_coordinator.rs` | Wake diagnostics constructors; wake reclaim driver/sweep functions; `wake_sweep_plan`, `partition_wake_sweep_candidates`, `wake_sweep_plan_from_selected`, `select_recoverable_sweep_candidates`, `wake_sweep_candidate_disposition`, `resumable_wake_sweep_disposition`, `reap_abandoned_sweep_candidates`, live-owner predicates/mappers, consumed-marker predicates, auto-wake helpers, wake-chain start helpers, process-spawn helpers, and tests | Source lines 55-1149; diff hunks 117-387 and 1094